# Where the packaged extension looks for the API. Baked into the bundle when it is
# compiled: the popup no longer has a field for it, so this is the only way to point
# a release at a host.
#
# Unset means a development compile — WXT falls back to http://localhost:3000 so CI
# stays green with nothing configured, and `wxt zip` refuses to package. The line is
# drawn at release, not earlier: an uncompressed output directory is not an artifact
# anyone ships.
#
# The WXT_ prefix is required. Only variables carrying it are exposed to the bundle
# as `import.meta.env.WXT_*`.
#
# Commented because the value below is the fallback src/settings.ts already
# applies, so a copy of this file does not need to carry it. Uncomment it only
# to point a build somewhere else — and for a release that somewhere else can
# never be localhost, which `prezip` rejects by name.
# WXT_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
